==== Installation direct to Flash ====

Once a serial (uartp **3.3v**) console has been established (see below for further details):

  - Download the ''...sysupgrade.bin'' image as shown above
  - Switch on the device and press ''t'' on the serial console until you get a prompt
  - Optionally backup OEM flash:(needs console log; output hex, not binary; takes one hour)<code> sf read 0x80800000 0x000000 0x1000000 
 md.b 0x80800000 0x1000000 </code>
  - Optionally backup OEM radio partition MTD7:(needs console log; output hex, not binary; see below why)<code> sf read 0x80800000 0xff0000 0x10000 
 md.b 0x80800000 0x10000 </code>
  - Optionally set the device's IP (defaults to 192.168.1.1):<code>setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1</code>
  - Optionally set the address of your TFTP server (defaults to 192.168.1.100):<code>setenv serverip 192.168.1.2</code>
  - Clear garbage data from RAM (not flash):<code>mw.b 0x80800000 0xff 0xf00000</code>
  - Download the image into RAM (not flash):<code>tftpboot 0x80800000 openwrt-19.07.4-lantiq-xrx200-tplink_vr200v-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin</code>
  - Erase the rootfs flash area:<code>sf erase 0x20000 0xf00000</code>
  - Write image to flash:<code>sf write 0x80800000 0x20000 0xf00000</code>\\ **Note:** depending on your terminal emulation settings you may not see when the flash is finished, you could try to "blindly" type the next command (should be rather safe)
  - Reboot:<code>reset</code>

Note: Instalation with the methods: "OEM firmware update", "Rescue Mode" and "tftp request" do not work.

==== Restore TP-LINK FW ====

Once a serial console has been established (see below for further details):
  - Obtain your firmware image. You need to strip the header off first: <code>dd if=orig.bin of=tplink.bin skip=257 bs=512</code>
  - Switch on the device and press **t** on the serial console until you get a prompt, then run commands similar to these:
    - Optionally set the device's IP (defaults to 192.168.1.1): <code>setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1</code>
    - Optionally set the address of your TFTP server (defaults to 192.168.1.100): <code>setenv serverip 192.168.1.2</code>
    - Download the image into RAM (**not flash**): <code>tftpboot 0x80800000 tplink.bin</code>
    - Erase the rootfs flash area:<code>sf erase 0x20000 0xf00000</code>
    - Write image to flash: <code>sf write 0x80800000 0x20000 0xf00000</code>
    - Reboot: <code>reset</code>

